NOT linked to those spell rows. Each is a special ability with its P.P.E. cost and duration (one minute per level). || PSIONICS: none printed; no psionics block. MAGIC: none; ability 6 says the class cannot learn other magic, stored as a restriction; no magic block. || SKILLS: Language: Quechua is printed with no percentage and is stored at the catalog base 50/5 (no native-language 98% is printed for this class, unlike the Line Maker''s Quechua 98%). Language two of choice as two Language: Other picks with no bonus. Basic Radio is Radio: Basic 45+15; Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45+15; Intelligence 32+10; Wilderness Survival 30+10; Tracking is Tracking (people) 25+10. W.P. Staff is granted (treat like W.P. Sword is a note). Hand to Hand: Expert changes to Martial Arts for one other skill; Assassin is not offered by the book. || RELATED: eight, plus one at 3, 6, 8, 11 and 13. Communications +5, Domestic +5, Espionage +10, Physical +5 (where applicable), Rogue +5, Technical +10, Wilderness +10; Medical First Aid, Paramedic or Holistic Medicine only; Military, Pilot, Pilot Related, Science and W.P. any; Electrical and Mechanical none (omitted). || SECONDARY: the book says three secondary skills at levels one, five and ten. Read as three at each of those levels (count 3, +3 at 5, +3 at 10); the other reading, one at each level, would be three in all. Same list without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: Pattern Staff (catalog pattern-staff). Two energy or rocket weapons of choice, typically a pistol and a rifle, as a choice of two from the Empire''s Inti-10, Inti-20, Illapa-1 and Illapa-5. A radio is the walkie-talkie-radio; ceremonial robes are ceremonial-robe x2; survival knife, survival kit, two sets of traveling clothes, backpack and first aid kit are catalog rows. Armor: none. || MONEY: printed 1D6x1000 credits (the OCR reads |D6x1000). || Sealed-armor damage is side_effects."
