## Lore

Rune warriors began with the ancient Nazca, whose line-making sorcerer-kings
needed soldiers able to stand against the Pucara, the red-skinned giants of the
Andes. Children, usually orphans, were raised in special camps, steeped in
magical energy and given permanent line drawings on their skin until they
became supernatural beings. Each also received a Pattern Staff, a weapon of
woven magical energy bound to its owner''s life.

These warriors led the campaigns that drove the giants underground. When Nazca
became part of the Empire of the Sun, the Incas trained the order in far
greater numbers. Today rune warriors guard priests and envoys, patrol the most
dangerous frontiers, and fight Arkhons, undead, guerrillas and bandits; a few
champions have been sent beyond the Empire and even across the Megaverse.

Outsiders from technological nations often laugh at the unarmored, spear-bearing
warriors in cloaks and loincloths. The warriors do not mind, since that
underestimation has cost many enemies dearly. Most of them tolerate technology
only when they must and trust their patterns first.

## GM Notes

Alignment: any, but usually good or unprincipled. There are no attribute
requirements; the book asks only for a will to fight evil, protect the innocent
or defend the Empire.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'rune-warrior');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'rune-warrior';

